nd have not wickedly departed from my God.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ%For all his judgments were before me,¦layout ‚¤textÙ,And I did not put away his statutes from me.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤text¾I was also upright before him,¦layout ‚¤textÙ%And I kept myself from mine iniquity.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙETherefore hath the LORD recompensed me according to my righteousness,¦layout ‚¤textÙ7According to the cleanness of my hands in his eyesight.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ2With the merciful thou wilt shew thyself merciful;¦layout ‚¤textÙ3With an upright man thou wilt shew thyself upright;¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ*With the pure thou wilt shew thyself pure;¦layout ‚¤textÙ4And with the froward thou wilt shew thyself froward.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ(For thou wilt save the afflicted people;¦layout ‚¤text¿But wilt bring down high looks.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤text¾For thou wilt light my candle:¦layout ‚¤textÙ+The LORD my God will enlighten my darkness.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ'For by thee I have run through a troop;¦layout ‚¤textÙ(And by my God have I leaped over a wall.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤text¿As for God, his way is perfect:¦layout ‚¤textÙNThe word of the LORD is tried: He is a buckler to all those that trust in him.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse$¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤text½For who is God save the LORD?¦layout ‚¤text¾Or who is a rock save our God?¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ(It is God that girdeth me with strength,¦layout ‚¤textºAnd maketh my way perfect.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ#He maketh my feet like hinds' feet,¦layout ‚¤textÙ#And setteth me upon my high places.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤text¼He teacheth my hands to war,¦layout ‚¤textÙ.So that a bow of steel is broken by mine arms.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ4Thou hast also given me the shield of thy salvation:¦layout ‚¤textÙLAnd thy right hand hath holden me up, and thy gentleness hath made me great.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ%Thou hast enlarged my steps under me,¦layout ‚¤textºThat my feet did not slip.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse$…¤book§chapter«first_verse%ªlast_verse*¦verses–„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ0I have pursued mine enemies, and overtaken them:¦layout ‚¤textÙ1Neither did I turn again till they were consumed.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ4I have wounded them that they were not able to rise:¦layout ‚¤text¾They are fallen under my feet.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ6For thou hast girded me with strength unto the battle:¦layout ‚¤textÙ9Thou hast subdued under me those that rose up against me.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ2Thou hast also given me the necks of mine enemies;¦layout ‚¤textÙ'That I might destroy them that hate me.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ,They cried, but there was none to save them:¦layout ‚¤textÙ-Even unto the LORD, but he answered them not.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ7Then did I beat them small as the dust before the wind:¦layout ‚¤textÙ/I did cast them out as the dirt in the streets.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse*…¤book§chapter«first_verse+ªlast_verse-¦verses“„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines”‚¤textÙ8Thou hast delivered me from the strivings of the people;¦layout ‚¤textÙ.And thou hast made me the head of the heathen:¦layout§quote_2‚¤text­A people whom¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ I have not known shall serve me.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse+„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ/As soon as they hear of me, they shall obey me:¦layout ‚¤textÙ.The strangers shall submit themselves unto me.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse,„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤text¾The strangers shall fade away,¦layout ‚¤textÙ(And be afraid out of their close places.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse-…¤book§chapter«first_verse.ªlast_verse2¦verses•„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ(The LORD liveth; and blessed be my rock;¦layout ‚¤textÙ+And let the God of my salvation be exalted.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse.„¥verse/¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤text»It is God that avengeth me,¦layout ‚¤textÙ!And subdueth the people under me.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse/„¥verse0¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ`He delivereth me from mine enemies: Yea, thou liftest me up above those that rise up against me:¦layout ‚¤textÙ,Thou hast delivered me from the violent man.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse0„¥verse1¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙBTherefore will I give thanks unto thee, O LORD, among the heathen,¦layout ‚¤text¿And sing praises unto thy name.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse1„¥verse2¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ(Great deliverance giveth he to his king;¦layout ‚¤textÙJAnd sheweth mercy to his anointed, to David, and to his seed for evermore.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse2